#! Symbols and comments for mdisasm.py (see its docstring for the format).
#! Regenerate the listing with:
#!   ../.venv/bin/python mdisasm.py monitor-183.bin --sym monitor-183.sym --speculate -o monitor-183.asm
%; =============================================================================
%;  Devtronix System Monitor 2.6 (183), 05/11/93  --  annotated disassembly
%;  Model 264 pipe-organ relay, Motorola 68000.  See README.md for the overview.
%; =============================================================================
%;
%;  Generated by mdisasm.py from monitor-183.bin (= monitor-183.raw with the two
%;  bytes of every word swapped; the disk and RAM store 16-bit words low byte
%;  first but strings in byte-address order, see ../boot-rom/README.md).
%;  Names and comments come from monitor-183.sym.  Not directly assemblable.
%;
%;  Addressing.  The image is loaded at $1032 by the boot ROM.  Its first
%;  instruction is `lea 0(pc),a5`, so A5 = (load address - $1032) = 0 and every
%;  variable is addressed as d16(a5): the first 4 KB of RAM.  Code calls other
%;  modules with `move.l #addr,d7 ; jsr (a5,d7.l)`; vectors are built the same
%;  way, so the image can be relocated (it is also loaded over the PC link).
%;
%;  System calls.  `moveq #n,d7 ; trap #0` calls the kernel: a round-robin task
%;  scheduler, a heap, a text-window system, console/modem I/O, a command-line
%;  parser and misc. helpers (table trap0_table at $356A, names T0 below).
%;  Some take a NUL-terminated string INLINE after the trap ($0B always; $03 and
%;  $35 when d6 bit 0 is set); the handler steps the return address past it.
%;  `moveq #n,d7 ; trap #1` is the disk/file service (table trap1_table at
%;  $3F48, names T1 below).  A3 points at the caller's file request block (see
%;  README.md "File request block"); (a3) receives the error code, Z = no error.
%;  `trap #3` with a6 -> {next.l, callback.l, ...} and d6 = delay in ticks
%;  schedules a callback on the 1 ms timing wheel.
%;
%;  Tasks (task_table at $A776, created by task_init): SCN console scanner, OPR
%;  operator (command line), FIL disk, CTL console-button commands, PLA player,
%;  REC recorder, STS status display, SNG song list, PCL PC link, DBG channel-B
%;  debug console.  Task block: +0 ready.w, +2 saved SP, +6 current window,
%;  +$A next task, +$E name[4], +$12 stack size, +$16 worst run time.
%;
%;  Labels: sys_NN / dsk_NN kernel entry points; tbl_XXXXX_n jump-table entries;
%;  spec_XXXXX code found by the speculative pass (unreferenced from traced code,
%;  reached through data structures); dat_XXXXX data referenced with lea.
%;
%;  I/O (short absolute addresses, all in $FFFFxxxx):
%;    $FE00      status display (boot ROM); $FE03/$FE06 read once at start
%;    $FE11..1F  MC6840 PTM on odd bytes, 800 kHz clock: T1 = 1 ms system tick
%;               (IRQ via vector $78), T2 = tempo pulse (96 per beat, latch =
%;               500000/BPM), T3 = one-shot pulse (written with movep at $FE1D)
%;    $FE21..3F  MC68681 DUART: A = terminal, B = modem/debug (IRQ vector $3C)
%;    $FF80/82   console scanner: data word / control word (input boards,
%;               output boards, successive-approximation A/D for analog inputs)
%;    $FF84/86   console scanner strobes cleared every tick
%;    $FFE0..E7  WD179x floppy, see ../boot-rom/README.md
%;    movec CACR Dimension-030 accelerator; its driver lives at $132DC
%;

